15 0 obj
<< /A 36 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating pathways of the immune response in the spleen, featuring red pulp and white pulp mechanisms. Left panel: T-Cell-Dependent Pathway shows interactions between dendritic cells \(DCs\), CD4 T cells, Tfh cells, B cells, and plasma cells producing immunoglobulin G \(IgG\). Right panel: T-Cell-Independent Pathway displays the activation of marginal zone B cells responding to damaged red blood cells, with detailed intracellular signaling involving receptors like IFNAR and molecules such as TYK2, JAK1, STAT1, and IRF7, leading to interferon-stimulated genes \(ISGs\) response.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 25 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 37 0 R /Alt (Graphic titled \215Key Determinants of RBC Alloimmunization\216 with an illustration of a human body receiving a blood transfusion. It lists factors influencing red blood cell alloimmunization: immunogenicity of RBC antigens, inflammation, donor age and reticulocyte content, underlying diseases, and transfusion variables. Each factor is detailed in separate text boxes explaining their impact on alloimmunization susceptibility and response.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
